# Frontend (Next.js)

The UI lives in **`web/`** (sibling of the Python `app/` package). Do not put Next.js inside `app/`.

Do not copy Vercel guidance into this file. Follow the installed skills:

| When | Skill | What to read |
|------|-------|----------------|
| Write, review, or refactor React/Next.js | `vercel-react-best-practices` | `SKILL.md`, then only the matching files under `.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/rules/` |
| Full compiled Vercel guide | same skill | `.agents/skills/vercel-react-best-practices/AGENTS.md` — **not** the repo-root `AGENTS.md` |
| After edits, with `next dev` running | `next-dev-loop` | Confirm the change at runtime via `/_next/mcp` and `agent-browser` |

# Constraints from those skills

* Prefer App Router patterns; apply Vercel rules by impact (waterfalls and bundle size first).
* `next-dev-loop` requires Next.js **16.3+** with Turbopack and `agent-browser` **>= 0.31.1**. If either is missing, tell the user how to upgrade and stop — do not fall back to grepping source as verification.
* Compile or type-check passing is not sufficient. Verify: compiles (`get_compilation_issues`), no runtime errors, intended UI behavior, React-level behavior when relevant.
* FastAPI stays the API. Browser clients call the BFF `web/app/api/support/[...path]`; do not reimplement graph or RAG logic in the UI.
* Customer portal is a live chat after email login (`portal_session` cookie). The BFF injects `X-Customer-Email` and SSE headers (`cache-control: no-cache`, `X-Accel-Buffering: no`).
* Support console live inbox: `/console/inbox` and `/console/inbox/[id]` with takeover. Do not add WebSockets.
* Assistant bubbles may render a tight markdown whitelist (`p ul ol li strong em code a`). Customer/human bubbles are plain text. Load `realtime-chat` before changing chat UI.
* Chat hook must not duplicate bubbles: fingerprint `assistant`/`human_agent` together, ignore EventSource while POST is in flight, do not upsert leftover draft after `done`. Invariants: `project-setup` `references/runtime-invariants.md`.
* Runtime verify with `next-dev-loop` (`/_next/mcp`). The user's Playwright MCP is allowed; `.cursor/mcp.json` stays empty (no product MCP).

# Language

* Code, comments, and filenames: **English**.
* Explain decisions to the user: **Portuguese**.
